==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*fuglaz}}. Cognate with {{etyl|ofs|-}} {{m|ofs|fugel}} ({{etyl|fy|-}} {{m|fy|fûgel}}), {{etyl|goh|-}} {{m|goh|fogal}} ({{etyl|de|-}} {{m|de|Vogel}}), {{etyl|osx|-}} {{m|osx|fugal}} ({{etyl|nds-de|-}} {{m|nds-de|Vagel|Vagel, Vogel}}), {{etyl|odt|-}} {{m|odt|fogal}} ({{etyl|nl|-}} {{m|nl|vogel}}), {{etyl|non|-}} {{m|non|fugl}} ({{etyl|sv|-}} {{m|sv|fågel}}, {{etyl|da|-}} {{m|da|fugl}}), {{etyl|got|-}} {{m|got|𐍆𐌿𐌲𐌻𐍃}}. The Germanic base is a variant of {{m|gem-pro|*flugla-||fly}}, compare {{m|gem-pro|*fleuganą}} ({{etyl|ang|-}} {{m|ang|flēogan}}).

